{pad:meta title='Comments'/}

<p>PAD has two comment forms. Both are taken out of the template before it is scanned, so a tag written inside one never runs and nothing of it reaches the output.</p>

<ul>
  <li><code>{pad:open/}# ... #{pad:close/}</code> - the original form</li>
  <li><code>{pad:open/}-- ... --{pad:close/}</code> - the form the editor kits highlight and toggle</li>
</ul>

{common:example 'fragments/comments_1'/}

<h2>Rules</h2>

<ul>
  <li>A comment closes at the first <code>#{pad:close/}</code> or <code>--{pad:close/}</code> after it, and may span lines.</li>
  <li><code>{pad:open/}--</code> must be followed by whitespace: a CSS custom property inside an {app:tag 'ignore'/} block, <code>:root{pad:open/}--gap:4px{pad:close/}</code>, is CSS and stays as it is.</li>
  <li><code>{pad:open/}#name{pad:close/}</code> is not a comment but the option sigil - the value of the tag option <code>name</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>See Also</h2>

<ul>
  <li>{app:manual 'ignore'/} - keep PAD from parsing braces</li>
</ul>
